        contaminants="In Dushanbe, treated water generally meets basic safety standards, but aging pipes leak and allow contamination. In rural areas, open irrigation channels (aryks) are sometimes used for drinking despite carrying agricultural runoff and animal waste. Seasonal flooding increases turbidity and bacterial contamination in mountain communities.",
        regional="Dushanbe has the most reliable supply, though quality varies by neighborhood. Khujand in the north has basic treatment but inconsistent delivery. In the Gorno-Badakhshan Autonomous Region (GBAO) &mdash; the remote Pamir highlands &mdash; communities rely on untreated spring and river water. The Fergana Valley towns face agricultural contamination.",
        tips=["Use bottled or boiled water throughout Tajikistan, including Dushanbe", "Carry a portable filter for travel in the Pamir Highway region", "Avoid drinking from irrigation channels (aryks) under any circumstances", "In homestays, accept offered tea &mdash; boiled water is safe"],
